cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DataMind in your research or applications, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "DataMind: A Verifiable Natural-Language Data Agent Powered by Snowflake and Google Gemma"
authors:
  - name: "DataMind Contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-18
url: "https://github.com/ArnavBallinCode/ZeroDay"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "snowflake"
  - "google-gemma"
  - "natural-language-to-sql"
  - "semantic-layer"
  - "data-agent"
  - "verifiable-ai"
  - "hacktoberfest"
  - "open-source"
abstract: >-
  DataMind is an open-source, verifiable natural-language data agent developed
  for ZeroDay OSS Hacktoberfest 2026. It pairs Google Gemma for semantic intent
  extraction with a deterministic SQL compiler and Snowflake execution engine,
  producing end-to-end auditability and cryptographically backed query receipts.
